I'll agree on reflection that the timeout is probably too low.  However 
attempting to melee a gelatinous cube is a bad idea no matter the 
circumstances, and (I feel) is even more true in the context from which 
the cube originates (D&D).  Of course, this ability makes the cube 
correspondingly more difficult and probably should be treated as such 
(part of my rationale for developing the patch is that I believe the 
vanilla representation of the cube is underpowered).

On the latter point, I can think of two options: have the cube only appear 
in later levels or simply leave it, hoping that novice adventurers will 
eventually pick up on not attempting to fight it hand-to-hand (akin to the 
unwritten floating eye rule).

In any case, I plan on waiting for more feedback before adjusting 
anything.  Thanks again for your help.

